{"book":10,"chapter":24,"context":{"chapter":24,"title":"The Census and the Threshing Floor","summary":"David orders a census of his fighting men, then feels guilty. Offered three punishments, he chooses to fall into God's hands, and a plague strikes. At the threshing floor of Araunah the plague stops; David buys the site, refusing to offer what cost him nothing, and builds an altar.","background":"The text does not explain why the census was wrong; many think it showed trust in military strength. The parallel account in 1 Chronicles 21:1 says Satan moved David to number Israel, and readers have long discussed how the two accounts relate. Araunah's threshing floor became the site of Solomon's temple on Mount Moriah (2 Chronicles 3:1).","customs":[{"term":"Threshing floor","verses":"24:18-24","note":"A flat, open rock surface on high ground, where grain was threshed and winnowed in the wind."}],"watchFor":["Even Joab objects to the census (v. 3).","'Let us fall now into the hand of the Lord; for his mercies are great' (v. 14).","'Neither will I offer... unto the Lord my God of that which doth cost me nothing' (v. 24)."],"connections":["Exodus 30:12","1 Chronicles 21:1","2 Chronicles 3:1","Genesis 22:2"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיֹּסֶף","vaiyosef","H3254","Hc/Vhw3ms","and it repeated"],["אַף","'af-","H639","HNcmsc","[the] anger of"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["לַחֲרוֹת","lacharot","H2734","HR/Vqcc","to burn"],["בְּיִשְׂרָאֵל","beyisra'el","H3478","HR/Npl","on Israel"],["וַיָּסֶת","vaiyaset","H5496","Hc/Vhw3ms","and he incited"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["דָּוִד","david","H1732","HNpm","David"],["בָּהֶם","bahem","H9038","HRd/Sp3mp","against <the> them"],["לֵאמֹר","lemor","H559","HR/Vqcc","<to> saying"],["לֵךְ","lekh","H1980","HVqv2ms","go"],["מְנֵה","meneh","H4487","HVqv2ms","count"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["יִשְׂרָאֵל","yisra'el","H3478","HNpl","Israel"],["וְאֶת","ve'et","H853","HC/To","and <obj.>"],["יְהוּדָה","yehudah","H3