st of Hareth (1 Chr. 29:29; 2 Chr. 29:25; 1 Sam. 22:5).","verses":13,"father":"","mother":"","v":[11,13,14,18,19]},{"id":"ornan_289","name":"Ornan","also":"Araunah","summary":"Agile; also called Ornan 1 Chr. 21:15, a Jebusite who dwelt in Jerusalem before it was taken by the Israelites. The destroying angel, sent to punish David for his vanity in taking a census of the people, was stayed in his work of destruction near a threshing-floor belonging to Araunah which was situated on Mount Moriah.","verses":17,"father":"","mother":"","v":[16,18,20,21,22,23,24]}],"places":[{"id":"beersheba_170","name":"Beersheba","kind":"City","lat":31.245,"lon":34.84068,"summary":"Well of the oath, or well of seven, a well dug by Abraham, and so named because he and Abimelech here entered into a compact (Gen. 21:31). On re-opening it, Isaac gave it the same name (Gen. 26:31-33).","verses":32,"v":[2,7,15]},{"id":"dan_323","name":"Dan","kind":"Region","lat":33.24856,"lon":35.65252,"summary":"The fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s maid (Gen. 30:6, “God hath judged me”, Heb. dananni).","verses":20,"v":[2,6,15]},{"id":"aroer_94","name":"Aroer","kind":"City","lat":31.9617,"lon":35.9115,"summary":"One of the towns built by the tribe of Gad (Num. 32:34) “before Rabbah” (Josh. 13:25), the Ammonite capital. It was famous in the history of Jephthah (Judg. 11:33) and of David (2 Sam. 24:5).","verses":6,"v":[5]},{"id":"jazer_628","name":"Jazer","kind":"City","lat":31.94353,"lon":35.72777,"summary":"He (God) helps, a city of the Amorites on the east of Jordan, and assigned, with neighbouring places in Gilead, to Gad (Num. 32:1, 35; Josh. 13:25).","verses":12,"v":[5]},{"id":"jordan_653","name":"Jordan","kind":"Water (River)","lat":33.18645,"lon":35.61916,"summary":"But besides these two historical fountains there is a third, called the Hasbany, which rises in the bottom of a valley at the western base of Hermon, 12 miles north of Tell-el-Kady.","verses":177,"v":[5]},{"id":"gilead_475","name":"Gilead","kind":"Region","lat":32.75,"lon":35.75,"summary":"Hill of testimony, (Gen. 31:21), a mountainous region east of Jordan. From its mountainous character it is called “the mount of Gilead” (Gen. 31:25).","verses":80,"v":[6]},{"id":"kadesh_662","name":"Tahtimhodshi","kind":"","lat":34.55833,"lon":36.52294,"summary":"The land of the newly inhabited, (2 Sam. 24:6). It is conjectured that, instead of this word, the reading should be, “the Hittites of Kadesh,” the Hittite capital, on the Orontes.","verses":1,"v":[6]},{"id":"sidon_1093","name":"Sidon","kind":"City","lat":33.56024,"lon":35.37121,"summary":"A fishery, a town on the Mediterranean coast, about 25 miles north of Tyre. It received its name from the “first-born” of Canaan, the grandson of Noah (Gen. 10:15, 19).","verses":30,"v":[6]},{"id":"judah_1280","name":"Judah","kind":"Region","lat":null,"lon":null,"summary":"Added from Digital Manna places-0611 (LPF sync 2026-10-13)","verses":27,"v":[7]},{"id":"negeb_885","name":"Negeb","kind":"Region","lat":30.25,"lon":34.75,"summary":"Heb. Negeb, that arid district to the south of Palestine through which lay the caravan route from Central Palestine to Egypt (Gen. 12:9; 13:1, 3; 46:1-6).","verses":36,"v":[7]},{"id":"tyre_1184","name":"Tyre","kind":"City","lat":33.26807,"lon":35.20936,"summary":"A rock, now es-Sur; an ancient Phoenician city, about 23 miles, in a direct line, north of Acre, and 20 south of Sidon. Sidon was the oldest Phoenician city, but Tyre had a longer and more illustrious history.","verses":52,"v":[7]},{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[8,16]}],"events":[{"id":"reign_of_david_159","title":"Reign of David","year":-1055,"summary":"Passage: 2 Samuel 2:1–24:25. People: David. Place: Hebron, Jerusalem. Laste